  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Mimeographed reproduction of hand-lettered poem and titles, illustrations, and typescript on individual leaves of a variety of brown, sand-colored, and white papers. Stapled and glued to endpapers and tied with cords to brown paper wrappers. Illustrations include mounted pink, yellow, and white decorated-paper cutouts. Collage on front wrapper includes a crescent-moon shaped mirror. Tied with purple and white cotton cord.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Part of a collection of handmade chapbooks, most with cords for hanging (literatura de cordel), published by Ediciones Vigía under the auspices of the Cuban Ministry of Culture.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Dibujos: Carlos Miguel Oliva. Diseño: Enrique Ramos"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Publication information from colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Consta de doscientos ejemplares numerados, firmados por su autora .... Para esta edición se utilizaron papeles craft, semicraft, bond, ecológico de la Papelera Cubana de Puentes Grandes, además de papel bond off set, donación de la Universidad de Lérida, España"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Condition of Art Library copy: no library markings, in protective enclosure.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="586" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
